lemma|question|explanation|distractor1|distractor2|distractor3
sich hinlegen|to lie down|Use the reflexive separable verb sich hinlegen for the action of lying down. Liegen describes already being in a lying position.|fliegen|lächeln|laden
Unterkunft|accommodation|Unterkunft is a feminine noun: die Unterkunft, plural Unterkünfte. German nouns start with a capital letter.|die Übung|der Urlaub|der Unfall
Urlaub|holiday / vacation|Urlaub means a holiday or vacation; the article is der.|die Schule|der Umkreis|die Übung
wenig|little / not much|Wenig describes a small quantity, as in wenig Zeit. Klein describes small size.|groß|viel|schnell
preisgünstig|inexpensive / good value|Preisgünstig contains ü and means inexpensive or good value, rather than expensive.|ungeliebt|vernünftig|teuer
episch|epic|Episch means epic, for example when describing a story. It is an adjective.|zaghaft|salzig|hektisch
renommiert|renowned / prestigious|Renommiert describes someone or something with an established good reputation.|erfinderisch|mangelhaft|unbekannt
sich einprägen|to memorise / commit to memory|Sich etwas einprägen means to commit something to memory. The reflexive pronoun is part of this construction.|suggerieren|niesen|revidieren
schwierig|difficult|Schwierig means difficult, as in eine schwierige Frage.|salzig|einfach|hell
krabbeln|to crawl (as a baby does)|Krabbeln describes crawling like a baby. Kraulen normally means swimming the crawl or gently scratching/petting.|darlegen|belegen|meistern
verboten|forbidden / prohibited|Verboten means forbidden or prohibited, as in Rauchen ist verboten.|verantwortlich|verlassen|erlaubt
begegnen|to encounter / meet|Begegnen means to encounter someone and takes the dative: einer Freundin begegnen.|backen|binden|bauen
langweilig|boring|Langweilig is the adjective boring. Langweilen is a verb and is not the required adjective here.|lustig|aufregend|hungrig
vermuten|to suspect / suppose|Vermuten expresses an assumption or suspicion, rather than certainty.|verstehen|vergessen|verkaufen
Meinung|opinion|Meinung is a feminine noun: die Meinung, plural Meinungen.|die Meldung|die Miete|die Reise
Werbung|advertising / advertisement|Werbung is a feminine noun and is spelled with ordinary e: die Werbung.|der Nachbar|der Nachruf|das Wappen
Hochzeit|wedding|Hochzeit means wedding. It is capitalized and takes die; the plural is Hochzeiten.|der Hagel|der Haken|die Handhabung
Gefühl|feeling|Gefühl is a neuter noun: das Gefühl, plural Gefühle.|die Farbe|die Gabel|das Gebäude
Hilfsmittel|an aid / assistive tool|Hilfsmittel is an aid or assistive tool. It is not a general equivalent of a medical cure or remedy.|das Zeichen|die Zahlung|der Zahn
zuordnen|to assign / match|Zuordnen means to assign or match something to something else, for example words to pictures.|zeichnen|trennen|reisen
mangelhaft|inadequate / deficient|Mangelhaft describes deficient quality or performance. It does not generally mean financially poor.|müde|hungrig|hell
abhängen von|to depend on|Abhängen von means to depend on, with a dative object after von.|abbauen|abdrucken|abbringen
besorgt|worried / concerned|Besorgt is the adjective worried. Besorgen is a verb meaning to obtain or take care of something.|ruhig|froh|müde
böse|evil (as in an evil king)|Böse can mean evil in this context; in other contexts it can mean angry or cross.|beeilt|freundlich|hektisch
Erfindung|invention|Erfindung is a feminine noun: die Erfindung, plural Erfindungen.|die Ehescheidung|die Ehrung|die Einbindung
fremd|foreign / unfamiliar|Fremd means foreign or unfamiliar, depending on the context.|vertraut|salzig|hell
dagegen|against it / against that|Dagegen refers back to something and means against it or against that. Gegen normally introduces its object directly.|dafür|dorthin|daneben
spüren|to feel / sense|Spüren means to feel or sense something, such as cold wind.|schrumpfen|betrachten|zeichnen
opfern|to sacrifice|Opfern is a verb: to sacrifice something, for example time. Opfer is the related noun.|streuen|streiten|sparen
erschrecken|to frighten / startle someone|In jemanden erschrecken, the verb is transitive: to frighten or startle someone.|einbilden|erklären|erinnern
belasten|to burden / put a strain on|Belasten is a verb meaning to burden or put a strain on. It is not the noun a burden.|ausstrecken|belohnen|entlasten
anhaltend|continuing / persistent|Anhaltend describes something that continues, such as rain or pain.|kurzfristig|plötzlich|selten
unerkannt|unrecognised / undetected|Unerkannt describes something that has not been recognised or detected.|unbedingt|bekannt|deutlich
Fach|subject (at school)|Fach means a school subject in this context: das Fach, plural Fächer.|die Fabel|der Fahrer|die Feier
Gabe|a gift / natural talent|Gabe can mean a natural gift or talent. A wrapped present is usually ein Geschenk; German Gift means poison.|das Defizit|der Donner|die Schwäche
Entrichtung|payment (formal, of a fee)|Entrichtung is a formal noun often used for payment of a fee or charge. Ordinary everyday payment is usually Zahlung.|die Verteilung|der Hagel|der Bestandteil
bezweifeln|to doubt|Bezweifeln is the verb to doubt. The noun doubt is Zweifel.|blitzen|bewältigen|bezahlen
zerplatzen|to burst / pop|Zerplatzen describes bursting or popping, for example a balloon.|erkennen|erklären|erwarten
hektisch|hectic|Hektisch describes a rushed, hectic situation or manner.|ruhig|stimmig|langsam
Nahrungsaufnahme|food intake|Nahrungsaufnahme is a feminine noun for taking in food. The noun begins with a capital letter.|die Verunsicherung|der Genuss|die Handlung
zerhacken|to chop up|Zerhacken means to chop something into pieces, as with herbs.|schildern|wiederkehren|widerspiegeln
vergnügt|cheerful / happy|Vergnügt describes someone who is cheerful or enjoying themselves.|finster|ruppig|verkrampft
tragfähig|viable / workable (of a proposal)|Tragfähig describes a workable or viable proposal, or something able to bear a load. Environmentally sustainable is usually nachhaltig.|einfühlsam|vordergründig|beträchtlich
zurück|back (direction)|Zurück is an adverb expressing movement back. The verb to return would require a verb such as zurückkommen.|zahlen|zwei|hier
hell|bright / light|Hell describes brightness or a light colour, as in ein helles Zimmer.|dunkel|halb|heiß
reisen|to travel|Reisen means to travel. Rechnen means to calculate, rufen to call and rennen to run.|rechnen|rufen|rennen
Wetter|weather|Weather is das Wetter. Wind and Wolke name specific weather-related things.|der Wind|die Wolke|der Wald
Frühstück|breakfast|Frühstück is the morning meal: das Frühstück.|das Abendessen|das Mittagessen|das Getränk
Geld|money|Geld means money and takes the article das.|das Gold|die Münze|die Marke
Wohnung|apartment / flat|Wohnung is a feminine noun meaning an apartment or flat: die Wohnung.|das Haus|das Zimmer|das Gebäude
verstehen|to understand|Verstehen means to understand, as in Ich verstehe die Frage.|verlieren|versuchen|vergessen
Lehrer|teacher (male)|Lehrer is the masculine form for a teacher. The feminine form is Lehrerin.|der Arzt|der Student|der Fahrer
Freund|friend (male)|Freund means a male friend and may mean boyfriend depending on context. Freundin is the feminine form.|der Feind|der Fremde|der Fahrer
Sprache|language|Sprache means language: die Sprache, plural Sprachen.|das Buch|das Wort|der Satz
Computer|computer|Computer is masculine: der Computer. Its plural is also Computer.|das Telefon|das Tablet|die Kamera
